/*
 * Declares the ListComprValue class.
 *
 * ListComprValue represents the generator-level form of a list comprehension.
 * During validation, list comprehensions are desugared into an implicit block
 * that performs iteration, filtering, and element construction. This class
 * stores that synthesized block so that later phases—such as implicit casting,
 * type inference, and template specialization—can still recover the structure
 * of the original comprehension.
 *
 * Unlike a normal block, a ListComprValue preserves the exact block that was
 * generated by the validator, ensuring that semantic transformations can be
 * applied consistently even after desugaring.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::scope::list_compr
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/scope/list_compr.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
